title: Detection Engineering Framework
message: >-
  If you use this framework, please cite it using the metadata in this file.
type: software
version: 2.1.1
date-released: "2026-09-26"
license: Apache-2.0
license-url: "https://github.com/Ke0xes/Detection-Engineering-Framework/blob/main/License"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Ke0xes/Detection-Engineering-Framework"
url: "https://ke0xes.github.io/Detection-Engineering-Framework/"

abstract: >-
  A lifecycle standard for building, governing and retiring security
  detections. The framework defines normative requirements across planning,
  technical feasibility, detection engineering, response engineering, delivery
  and improvement, together with a three-level conformance model, machine-
  readable schemas for detection and use case metadata, and a reference
  implementation that enforces conformance in continuous integration. It
  requires two-way traceability from business drivers to telemetry, treats
  response engineering as a co-equal phase, and defines Vendor Agnostic Logic
  as a platform-independent correlation layer above portable rule formats.

